+### UE-20 refuses float-model production closures
+
+The new regression was run before the guard was implemented. With the actual
+Prelude loaded, `certify::mark` admitted `direct`, `transitive` and `integer`;
+`float_model_closures_are_refused_before_export_ue_20` failed because only
+`integer` should enter the production request. The guard restored the expected
+result. The same test exercises `production`, the kappa-keyed `refusals.toml`,
+and a batch selecting only the refused transitive root. Removing the guard
+recreates that defect.
+
+A second test executes the actual Prelude with its arbitrary-size test evaluator
+and records intermediates above 64 bits while checking the final float bits:
+binary64 multiplication 105/106, division 160, FMA 105, square-root search 325,
+addition alignment 103; binary32 division 73 and square-root search 153.
+`cargo test --offline --locked -p uorust --lib -- --nocapture` passed all 147
+library tests on 2026-11-16 with cached Rust 1.97.1.
+`cargo test --offline --locked -p uorust --test cli` also passed all 12 CLI
+tests; the four `repo-conformance --test bdd` meta-gate tests passed.
+`cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` passed.
+
+`scripts/probe-numeric-export.sh` provides the independent production probe. It
+exports only the exact Nat multiplication primitive used for the significand
+product, not a complete IEEE root. On LexLean 0.4.0 with binary SHA-256
+`9cba65a6cf2db6c1afc24c60d98621409c6f7eb9a1dcb99298bb658310f6e5d6`,
+the package was kernel-checked, `verify-artifact` replayed its bindings, and the
+unaltered generated Rust was compiled by Rust 1.97.1 to native and import-free
+Wasm. Both returned explicit `Overflow` for `2^52 * 2^52` and
+`(2^53-1) * (2^53-1)`, while zero, `u64::MAX * 1` and `2^23 * 2^23` controls
+succeeded. This is checked failure, not silent corruption. The bundle result ID
+was `1d5242cc9705d62484e05139ec5548d40a773009dcdb3ec3184dc230cfc215ba`.
+The source-free replay explicitly does not rerun Lean elaboration, axiom audit,
+leanchecker or extraction; those were part of the preceding production build.
+
+This diagnostic SDK matches the game's d6c263a7 image pin and inventory, not
+UORust's c74e492a patched-image pin. `xtask check-model --write` regenerated
+CONFORMANCE.md; `xtask validate` passed model, errors, deferral and dependency
+checks, then correctly refused the SDK inventory mismatch. The complete
+`just vv` acceptance boundary still requires UORust's exact pinned SDK; no lock
+was changed to bypass that check. This evidence is not release acceptance.
+
+The final UE-20 coverage rerun additionally passed qualified Behavior and
+Prelude-alias paths, helper-free bit identity, and the width-64 conversion
+mask (`floatToNat(11,52,64,1.0)` returns 1 with a 65-bit intermediate). This
+refines coverage without changing the production guard or claiming full
+float export. The two focused tests passed after these additions.
